## Foundational Axiom — Civilization Must Remain Interruptible

**No intelligence — human, institutional, or artificial — should become non-correctable.**

This is not a philosophical preference. It is the minimum structural condition for civilizational survivability. A state that cannot be reformed, a corporation that cannot be dissolved, an AI system that cannot be halted, a founder who cannot be replaced, a governance body that cannot be audited — each represents the same failure mode at a different scale: the elimination of the correction mechanism.

Every pillar in this doctrine is a derivation of this single principle. The principle governs AGI systems, private corporations, founder-controlled laboratories, national governments, and — critically — the governance institutions created by this framework itself. The recursive application is not a rhetorical flourish. It is the deepest structural commitment of the doctrine: that the apparatus built to enforce interruptibility must itself remain interruptible.

An interruptible civilization is the only kind that survives indefinitely. All others eventually encounter a condition they cannot self-correct from, and what they encounter at that moment determines whether the failure is recoverable.

