## Final Principle

The objective was never to find the right genius and trust them forever. That is not governance — it is prayer dressed as policy.

The objective is to build systems in which even imperfect humans, operating under ordinary incentives and ordinary cognitive limitations, cannot easily destroy the future. Systems that are robust to selfishness, to competitive pressure, to the compression of time horizons under stress, and to the ordinary human tendency to protect what one has built from the corrections it may need.

That is how civilization survives.

Not by heroes. Not by manifestos. Not by alignment commitments alone.

By architecture that survives contact with power — and that, when it fails, was designed from the beginning to be correctable.

